title: A Social Channel to the PiS Cabinet
subtitle: Lower hostility around material policy—and let the liberal opposition call it collusion.
new-page: true
is-card: true
# Compatibility card for held saves. New draws build this relationship through
# Party Affairs → Inter-Party Relations instead of duplicating it here.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and government_party = "pis" and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_pis_social_channel_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_pis_social_channel_timer = 4
card-image: img/poland/cards/negotiate-government.webp

= A social channel to the PiS cabinet

PiS hostility is **[+ government_negotiation_hostility +]/100**. Its
**[+ pis_dominant_wing +]** currently sets the public line. A regular channel
on wages, pensions and public services can make conflict less automatic, but
[? if third_way_active: KO and the Third Way will treat every meeting as an
attempt to divide the opposition.?][? if not third_way_active and p2050_emerged:
KO, Poland 2050 and PSL will each treat every meeting as an attempt to divide
the opposition.?][? if not third_way_active and not p2050_emerged: KO and PSL
will each treat every meeting as an attempt to divide the opposition.?]

- @protocol
- @briefings
- @close_channel

@protocol
title: Propose a standing social-policy protocol
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Hostility −12; PiS relation +8; solidarists +5. [? if third_way_active: Relations with KO and the Third Way fall.?][? if not third_way_active and p2050_emerged: Relations with KO, Poland 2050 and PSL fall.?][? if not third_way_active and not p2050_emerged: Relations with KO and PSL fall.?]
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A standing policy team requires one resource.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.government_negotiation_hostility -= 12;
Q.pis_negotiation_hostility_relief += 12;
Q.negotiation_capital += 2;
Q.pis_relation += 8;
Q.pis_solidarist_share += 5;
Q.pis_market_hardliner_share -= 5;
Q.pis_accept_social += 6;
Q.pis_accept_market -= 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 4;
Q.p2050_relation -= 3;
Q.psl_relation -= 2;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
Q.united_right_cohesion -= 4;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 2;
for (const id of ["solidarna", "pis_security", "pis_culture"]) {
    const current = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
        return record.id == id;
    });
    if (current) {
        current.cohesion -= 3;
        current.grievance_memory += 8;
    }
}
const welfare = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record.id == "pis_welfare";
});
if (welfare) {
    welfare.relation += 8;
    welfare.cohesion += 2;
}
Q.last_policy_stage = "Standing opposition-government protocol";
Q.last_policy_authority = "PiS cabinet retains implementation authority";
Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "A standing social channel divides PiS and the parliamentary opposition";
!}

The protocol names no coalition and promises no confidence votes. It does make
the welfare-conservative current the PiS gatekeeper for talks with Lewica.
Market liberals outside PiS denounce the arrangement; the culture-war and
sovereigntist right denounce it from inside the governing camp.

- #poland_card_finish


@briefings
title: Hold bill-by-bill technical briefings
subtitle: Free. Hostility −5; PiS relation +3; a smaller solidarist shift brings a smaller opposition cost.
on-arrival: government_negotiation_hostility -= 5; pis_negotiation_hostility_relief += 5; negotiation_capital += 1; pis_relation += 3; pis_solidarist_share += 2; pis_market_hardliner_share -= 2; pis_accept_social += 2; ko_relation -= 1; p2050_relation -= 1; psl_relation -= 1; government_coalition_dissent += 1; united_right_cohesion -= 1; progressives_dissent += 1; last_policy_stage = "Technical consultation"; last_policy_authority = "PiS cabinet retains implementation authority"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Technical social-policy briefings lower the temperature across the aisle"

The meetings produce shared language and fewer automatic refusals, not a bill.
The modest scale gives both sides room to deny that a durable alignment exists.

- #poland_card_finish


@close_channel
title: Refuse to normalise the PiS cabinet
subtitle: Keep opposition alignment; hostility +2 and PiS relation −2.
on-arrival: government_negotiation_hostility += 2; pis_negotiation_hostility_relief -= 2; pis_relation -= 2; ko_relation += 2; p2050_relation += 1; progressive_credibility += 2; progressives_dissent -= 1; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "Lewica refuses a standing channel to the PiS cabinet"

The line is clear and the next negotiation begins from a colder room.

- #poland_card_finish
